-- title:
--   Valuation subrings over a DVR in a separable extension are discrete with uniformiser π
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $M$ be fields with $M$ a $K$-algebra, and let $O$ be a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring together with an $O$-algebra structure on $M$. Assume the structure map $O \to M$ is injective, and that every element $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,M\,c$ ($c \in K$) lies in the image of $O \to M$. Let $E$ be a subfield of $M$ each of whose elements $x$ satisfies `IsSeparable K x`, i.e. the minimal polynomial of $x$ over $K$ is separable (so $E/K$ is separable algebraic), and assume the subfield of $M$ generated by the union of the image of $O$ and $E$ is all of $M$. Let $V$ be a valuation subring of $M$ containing the image of every $b \in O$, and such that $V$ is centred on the maximal ideal of $O$ in the sense that the valuation attached to $V$ satisfies $v(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,O\,M\,b) < 1$ for every $b$ in the maximal ideal of $O$. Finally let $\pi \in O$ be irreducible. Then $V$ is a principal ideal ring, $V \neq M$, and the maximal ideal of the local ring $V$ is the ideal of $V$ generated by the image of $\pi$.
--
--   This is the statement that a valuation subring of a field generated over a discrete valuation ring $O$ by a separable algebraic constant extension, lying over the maximal ideal of $O$, is again a discrete valuation ring with the same uniformiser; the three conjuncts are exactly the data needed to treat $V$ as a discrete place of $M$. It is used in the analysis of orders of vanishing at places of modular curves, where a place over a supersingular point is compared with the height-one prime of a node ring beneath it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_isPrincipalIdealRing_and_maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_irreducible.lean

